\par\par \b \uc2 2nd UPDATE: Polish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\uc2  To Weaken Zloty\b0\par\par\uc2 430 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2010\par 14:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (Adds comment, detail.) \par  \par    By Malgorzata Halaba and Marynia Kruk \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Friday afternoon to weaken the rapidly strengthening zloty, for the first time since its floatation in April 2000.\f28 \par \par \uc2 And while the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably only weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  temporarily, economists agree it has shown that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to be an active player and may come back to the market when needed.\par \par \uc2 "The move is of a signaling nature," Mateusz Szczurek, chief economist at \uc2 ING Bank Slaski\uc2 , said in a note. "But it does signal the readiness and capability to act, not something obvious after years of idleness."\par \par \uc2 Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move will "ease" the scope of the strengthening, added Maciej Reluga, chief economist at \uc2 Bank Zachodni WBK\uc2  in Warsaw.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not change the trend," he said. "But the average zloty rate will be slightly higher."\par \par \uc2 Also, because of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the zloty rate "will not be a one-way bet any longer," Reluga added.\par \par \uc2 "We maintain an overall positive view on the PLN in a longer term perspective," Nordea said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Among positive drivers Nordea listed the relatively healthy economic outlook, potential privatization revenue and polls favoring a ruling Civic Platform president in the presidential elections in the autumn.\par \par \uc2 "Today's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to be followed by more verbal and actual \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rate hikes might be postponed if the PLN remains strong," Nordea said.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought an undisclosed amount of euros at PLN3.8450-PLN3.8500, according to a dealer at \uc2 ING Bank Slaski\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Thus the bank implemented its earlier warning that it's "technologically and psychologically" prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the excessive strengthening of the zloty, which could hamper economic growth.\par \par \uc2 The zloty has been highly volatile over the past two years, reaching its strongest level ever at PLN3.20 against the euro in July 2008 and weakening dramatically during the global financial crisis to near its all-time weakest level of PLN4.92 against the euro in February 2009.\par \par \uc2 Over the past 14 months, the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has regained much of its pre-crisis strength. At 0539 GMT Friday, it stood at PLN3.8468 to the euro. At 1149 GMT, the zloty was at PLN3.8826 to the euro from PLN3.8454 early Friday.\par \par \uc2 -By Malgorzata Halaba and Marynia Kruk, Dow Jones Newswires; +4822 447-2430;\par \par \uc2 malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com [ 09-04-10 1240GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100409e649001d7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
