\par\par \b \uc2 DJ MARKET TALK: Interest Rate Futures Lower As Inventories Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 987 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2010\par 16:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1414 GMT [Dow Jones] U.S. rate futures well-positioned for unexpected boost in wholesale inventories reported Friday, seen as sign of growing consumer demand. Eurodollar futures prices continue lower, with Sep contract recently off 2 BPs and Dec down 3.5 BPs. Quarterly 2011 contracts down by as much as 6 BPs. Long-end Tsy futures also edge lower with Jun 10-yr note contract off 6/32 at 115-20 and Jun 30-yr bond futures down 8/32 at 115-05, the latter hitting a new session low just before inventory data release. (jacob.bunge@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1412 GMT [Dow Jones] The continued onslaught of Treasury auctions, including this week's $82 bln new government bond sales, fills demand for collateral in the overnight repo market. All maturities trade with rates ranging between 0.15 and 0.25%. The GC repo rate, the market's benchmark, trading at 0.26%, compared with the zero-0.25% range for the fed-funds target rate. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1404 GMT [Dow Jones] Wholesale inventories jumped 0.6% in February, double the 0.3% increase expected. January's inventory level revised to an increase of 0.1%, rather than the 0.2% drop originally reported. Inventory gain looks like a response to higher demand--not an unexpected buildup of unwanted goods--as wholesale sales rose 0.8% in February.\par \par \uc2 (kathleen.madigan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1359 GMT [Dow Jones] Safe-haven Treasurys are losing their luster. Bond yields hit session highs as Medley, an influential think tank, says that EU has reaches agreement for funding terms for Greece. Euro got a strong boost on the news while US stocks are higher. DJIA up 41. Two-year note's yield is up 3.7 BP at 1.105%. The 10-year note's yield is 2.7 BP higher at 3.923% and the 30-year bond's yield is 1.5 BP higher at 4.774%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1354 GMT [Dow Jones] Scotia Capital has changed its call for the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  and now forecasts it will hike by 25 bps at its June 1 policy date. The bank is conditionally committed to keeping its key overnight target rate at the lowest possible level of 0.25% until the end of 2Q. Scotia now forecasts the bank will hike by a cumulative 275 bps by 3Q of 'll. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1352 GMT [Dow Jones] The euro, near Y125.15, is breaking down on intraday trading below Y125.46. A move below Y125.09 would be the signal for dip to test Y125.02. If trades are stopped above Y125.20 look for a revisit of Y125.46 resistance.\par \par \uc2 (stephen.cox@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1348 GMT [Dow Jones] Interest rate futures prices begin to slide in midmorning trade as U.S. stocks firm. Sep Eurodollar futures down 2 BPs at 99.465 with Dec contract off 3 BPs at 99.17. Heavier selling in 2011-dated Eurodollars, with prices 3.5 to 4.5 BPs lower across the curve. June 10-yr note futures recently 5/32 lower at 115-21, while June 30-yr bond futures down 6/32 at 115-07. (jacob.bunge@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1343 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD hit an intraday high at 1.3431 from 1.3349 late Thu amid a decline in yield spreads of Greece's government bonds as worries about sovereign debt risk subsided. (fabio.alves@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1332 GMT [Dow Jones] The 10-year Treasury yield is likely to be capped below 4% in the near term, says William O'Donnell at RBS Securities. "The Treasury market passed a stern test this week and the outcome is a painful one for trend-junkies and the positively convex: rate ranges live on," says O'Donnell. He looks for the 10-year note's yield to trade between 3.700% and 4.000% in the coming month, adding that he would "buy dips to range support." The 10-year yield briefly broke above 4% Monday but has since trading below that level. In recent trade, it is 3.91%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1335 GMT [Dow Jones] Polish Treasury bonds are stronger following Thursday's losses as global sentiment improves, fueling gains on local stocks and bonds, a Warsaw-economist says. He expects gains to continue Monday as Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduces risk of a similar action in the near term. 2-year paper is at 4.50% from 4.62% Thursday; 5-year at 5.17% from 5.23%; 10-year at 5.62% from 5.68%. EUR/PLN at 3.8800 from 3.8390; USD/PLN at 2.9025 from 2.8673. (marek.strzelecki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1329 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday may be followed by further verbal and actual \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nordea says. Should the zloty remain strong, the country's rate-setting council may postpone interest rate hikes, Nordea adds. EUR/PLN now at 3.8757 from 3.8390 early Friday. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1320 GMT [Dow Jones] CAD has been little affected by news that Russia hasn't yet added Canadian-dollar assets to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's third-largest. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Sergei Ignatyev said Friday that problems with financial "infrastructure" have prevented CAD investments. Bank officials said last year they were planning such a move. USD is currently around 1.0054, below session high at 1.0081 and above low at 0.9993, according to EBS via CQG. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 09, 2010 10:15 ET (14:15 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100409e649003kj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
