\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Sell-Off Takes Shape In Rate Futures\b0\par\par\uc2 1,104 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2010\par 15:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1348 GMT [Dow Jones] Interest rate futures prices begin to slide in midmorning trade as U.S. stocks firm. Sep Eurodollar futures down 2 BPs at 99.465 with Dec contract off 3 BPs at 99.17. Heavier selling in 2011-dated Eurodollars, with prices 3.5 to 4.5 BPs lower across the curve. June 10-yr note futures recently 5/32 lower at 115-21, while June 30-yr bond futures down 6/32 at 115-07. (jacob.bunge@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1343 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD hit an intraday high at 1.3431 from 1.3349 late Thu amid a decline in yield spreads of Greece's government bonds as worries about sovereign debt risk subsided. (fabio.alves@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1332 GMT [Dow Jones] The 10-year Treasury yield is likely to be capped below 4% in the near term, says William O'Donnell at RBS Securities. "The Treasury market passed a stern test this week and the outcome is a painful one for trend-junkies and the positively convex: rate ranges live on," says O'Donnell. He looks for the 10-year note's yield to trade between 3.700% and 4.000% in the coming month, adding that he would "buy dips to range support." The 10-year yield briefly broke above 4% Monday but has since trading below that level. In recent trade, it is 3.91%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1335 GMT [Dow Jones] Polish Treasury bonds are stronger following Thursday's losses as global sentiment improves, fueling gains on local stocks and bonds, a Warsaw-economist says. He expects gains to continue Monday as Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduces risk of a similar action in the near term. 2-year paper is at 4.50% from 4.62% Thursday; 5-year at 5.17% from 5.23%; 10-year at 5.62% from 5.68%. EUR/PLN at 3.8800 from 3.8390; USD/PLN at 2.9025 from 2.8673. (marek.strzelecki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1329 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday may be followed by further verbal and actual \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nordea says. Should the zloty remain strong, the country's rate-setting council may postpone interest rate hikes, Nordea adds. EUR/PLN now at 3.8757 from 3.8390 early Friday. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1320 GMT [Dow Jones] CAD has been little affected by news that Russia hasn't yet added Canadian-dollar assets to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's third-largest. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Sergei Ignatyev said Friday that problems with financial "infrastructure" have prevented CAD investments. Bank officials said last year they were planning such a move. USD is currently around 1.0054, below session high at 1.0081 and above low at 0.9993, according to EBS via CQG. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1309 GMT [Dow Jones] Argentina is leading a rebound in emerging market bonds as stock futures point to stable risk appetite after sessions of profit-taking amid fears over Greece's debt crisis. Risk premium on \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's Emerging Market Bond Index Global is 3 bps tighter at 250 bps over Tsys, although its index is down 0.03%. Argentina is 20 bps tighter to 617 bps over Tsys, although its index too is down 0.64%, as investors await a possible debt-swap re-opening next week. Market benchmark bond, Brazil's Global 2040, is flat at 133 7/8 bid, according to Reuters. (riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1300 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 ING Bank Slaski\uc2  recommends closing short EUR/PLN positions "for now," following the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The bank's move, which is of a symbolic nature, could slow down the zloty appreciation process, especially when combined the Greek crisis still unfolding, ING says. EUR/PLN now at 3.8780 from 3.8390 early Friday. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1259 GMT [Dow Jones] Canadian short-term interests rates eased a few basis points and CAD retreated after weaker-than-expected March jobs data Fri, says Marc Chandler, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 . "While this immediate market reaction is understandable, the larger arguments for a Canadian rate hike and a strong Canadian dollar remain intact," he says. It would probably require a break of 1.0140-80 to begin shaking out CAD longs, Chandler says. "Near-term consolidation may be the most likely near-term scenario. If range trading does emerge, we are still more comfortable taking advantage of pullbacks in C$ to accumulate," he adds. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1256 GMT [Dow Jones] The MBS market has taken the Fed exit in stride so far, said analysts at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  in a research note. But the likelihood of risk premiums widening still remains, especially in the lower coupons that were favored by the Fed. Some of the cash on the sidelines, specifically banks and foreign investors, entered the market as prices went down.\par \par \uc2 (prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1255 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  revises its Hungary policy rate forecasts to 5.00% for end-2010, based on the Taylor rule, from its previous 5.50%, which is also the current level. Revises its HUF forecasts, however, stronger as economic and financial normalization and policy continuity will help reduce the risk premium of Hungarian assets, which should be HUF supportive. Sees EUR/HUF at 265, 265, 255 in 3, 6, and 12 months, respectively, from the previous 270, 275, and 275. Adds the new forecasts are contingent on key assumptions of "policy continuity" after parliamentary elections and sustained global financial and economic stabilization. Sees the policy rate climbing back again to 5.50% by the end of 2011. EUR/HUF is 267.10. (margit.feher@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1245 GMT[Dow Jones] Friday morning finds fed funds futures getting more optimistic that the Federal Reserve will start raising its benchmark interest rate in the 4Q. Oct fed funds contract, down 0.5 BP just after mkt open, sees 34% chance of the fed funds rate rising to 0.5% from current near-zero level following Sept. 21 FOMC meeting. Nov contract, recently down 1.5 BP, priced for 72% chance of the key rate rising when FOMC meets Nov. 2 to 3. That's up from 68% chance seen at Thursday's mkt close.(jacob.bunge@dowjones.com) [ 04-09-10 0949ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100409e64900091\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
