\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Polish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  May  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  Again -Nordea\b0\par\par\uc2 1,143 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2010\par 15:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1329 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday may be followed by further verbal and actual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Nordea says. Should the zloty remain strong, the country's rate-setting council may postpone interest rate hikes, Nordea adds. EUR/PLN now at 3.8757 from 3.8390 early Friday. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1320 GMT [Dow Jones] CAD has been little affected by news that Russia hasn't yet added Canadian-dollar assets to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's third-largest. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Sergei Ignatyev said Friday that problems with financial "infrastructure" have prevented CAD investments. Bank officials said last year they were planning such a move. USD is currently around 1.0054, below session high at 1.0081 and above low at 0.9993, according to EBS via CQG. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1309 GMT [Dow Jones] Argentina is leading a rebound in emerging market bonds as stock futures point to stable risk appetite after sessions of profit-taking amid fears over Greece's debt crisis. Risk premium on \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's Emerging Market Bond Index Global is 3 bps tighter at 250 bps over Tsys, although its index is down 0.03%. Argentina is 20 bps tighter to 617 bps over Tsys, although its index too is down 0.64%, as investors await a possible debt-swap re-opening next week. Market benchmark bond, Brazil's Global 2040, is flat at 133 7/8 bid, according to Reuters. (riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1300 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 ING Bank Slaski\uc2  recommends closing short EUR/PLN positions "for now," following the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The bank's move, which is of a symbolic nature, could slow down the zloty appreciation process, especially when combined the Greek crisis still unfolding, ING says. EUR/PLN now at 3.8780 from 3.8390 early Friday. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1259 GMT [Dow Jones] Canadian short-term interests rates eased a few basis points and CAD retreated after weaker-than-expected March jobs data Fri, says Marc Chandler, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 . "While this immediate market reaction is understandable, the larger arguments for a Canadian rate hike and a strong Canadian dollar remain intact," he says. It would probably require a break of 1.0140-80 to begin shaking out CAD longs, Chandler says. "Near-term consolidation may be the most likely near-term scenario. If range trading does emerge, we are still more comfortable taking advantage of pullbacks in C$ to accumulate," he adds. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1256 GMT [Dow Jones] The MBS market has taken the Fed exit in stride so far, said analysts at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  in a research note. But the likelihood of risk premiums widening still remains, especially in the lower coupons that were favored by the Fed. Some of the cash on the sidelines, specifically banks and foreign investors, entered the market as prices went down.\par \par \uc2 (prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1255 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  revises its Hungary policy rate forecasts to 5.00% for end-2010, based on the Taylor rule, from its previous 5.50%, which is also the current level. Revises its HUF forecasts, however, stronger as economic and financial normalization and policy continuity will help reduce the risk premium of Hungarian assets, which should be HUF supportive. Sees EUR/HUF at 265, 265, 255 in 3, 6, and 12 months, respectively, from the previous 270, 275, and 275. Adds the new forecasts are contingent on key assumptions of "policy continuity" after parliamentary elections and sustained global financial and economic stabilization. Sees the policy rate climbing back again to 5.50% by the end of 2011. EUR/HUF is 267.10. (margit.feher@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1245 GMT[Dow Jones] Friday morning finds fed funds futures getting more optimistic that the Federal Reserve will start raising its benchmark interest rate in the 4Q. Oct fed funds contract, down 0.5 BP just after mkt open, sees 34% chance of the fed funds rate rising to 0.5% from current near-zero level following Sept. 21 FOMC meeting. Nov contract, recently down 1.5 BP, priced for 72% chance of the key rate rising when FOMC meets Nov. 2 to 3. That's up from 68% chance seen at Thursday's mkt close.(jacob.bunge@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1244 GMT [Dow Jones] Markets might live and breathe by jobs numbers, as reflected in the selling of CAD after weak March data, but central banks don't, says Stewart Hall, market strategist at HSBC Securities Canada. Next Monday's \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  quarterly business outlook survey is more important to Canadian monetary policy than today's jobs data, he says. "While the BoC may be inclined to dismiss the sawtoothed-like movements of the jobs numbers, it will indeed pay particular attention to any hints at capacity constraints in the economy or changes in inflation expectations found in its [survey]," Hall says. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1241 GMT [Dow Jones] Friday's Swedish data, industrial production and orders, were altogether better than expected, says Swedbank. "The overriding news in today\u180\'00\'B4s report is in our view a sharp acceleration in new orders, especially new export orders. The year-on-year changes are now for both series almost at a decade all-time-high." Adds that this is a solid sign that previous strong indicator data start to materialize in actual hard data. Sweden's two-year bond yield trades unchanged at 1.52%, while the 10-year bond yield trades two basis points higher at 3.19%. (karl.bruze@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1239 GMT [Dow Jones] Norwegian inflation did not collapse during the recession, but it's retreating significantly now, says Handelsbanken (SHB), following Friday's inflation data release. Notes that \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2 's rate forecast implies a new hike on May 5. Adds: "We already had doubts about that. Today's data support that doubt and makes us aim rather for June 23." EUR/\uc2 NOK\uc2  trades at 7.9395. (karl.bruze@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1231 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasury prices are lower as anxiety over Greece's debt woes subsides. Riskier assets are doing better with the yield premium of Greek government debt over German bunds tightening slightly and US stock futures higher. The only US data is the release of wholesale inventories at 10 a.m. EDT. Two-year note's yield is flat at 1.089%. The 10-year note's yield is up 1.4 bps at 3.910% and the 30-year bond's yield is little changed at 4.761%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com) [ 04-09-10 0929ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100409e6490008s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
