\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW 3-Polish c.bank says  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  on  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , zloty down\b0\par\par\uc2 397 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2010\par 14:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, April 9 (Reuters) - The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday for the first time since the introduction of a free float in Poland, sending the zloty down by 1 percent immediately afterwards [ID:nWSF008907].\par \par \uc2 For the main story, please double click: [ID:nWSF008904] [ID:nWSF008905] .\par \par \uc2 Poland's government welcomed the move, Deputy Finance Minister Dominik Radziwill told Reuters. [ID:nWSF008906]\par \par \uc2 Following are analysts' comments:\par \par \uc2 KOON CHOW, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  STRATEGIST AT BARCLAYS CAPITAL\par \par \uc2 "We expect more noise on spot (...) but we remain confident in the medium-term uptrend in the zloty. We think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to slow the pace of zloty appreciation so as not to imperil the cautious cyclical recovery."\par \par \uc2 "This is a stance of many emerging market economies. We do not believe that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to drive the zloty weaker on a trend basis (not that we think they can) given the implications that a weak zloty would have on the external debt metrics of the government and of course on inflation as well."\par \par \uc2 PETER ATTARD MONTALTO, ECONOMIST AT NOMURA INTERNATIONAL\par \par \uc2 "NBP (National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) said to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in market is a break from past when the NBP was much more risk averse about getting involved in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This is being led by management board... not the MPC who no doubt will have something to say about it on wires shortly.\par \par \uc2 "For this reason it is possible that they can still hike rates later this year given MPC conflict and separation from management board. That said, it clearly would look very odd to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and hiking so the MPC may well be backed into a corner on this."\par \par \uc2 RAFAL BENECKI, SENIOR ECONOMIST AT \uc2 ING BANK SLASKI\par \par \uc2 "This comes after some earlier comment, so it gives credence to verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We should note, however, that this is a battle with our own success because the zloty's rise in the last three months is a result of the large demand for Polish bonds from abroad, as well as privatisation inflows."\par \par \uc2 "In the short term the effects of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will certainly be visible, but all we can expect is a slower pace of the zloty's rise." (Compiled by Gabriela Baczynska)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-ZLOTY/ (INSTANT VIEW 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|PX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100412e649000u8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
