\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervenes \highlight\uc2  to curb zloty, sets precedent\b0\par\par\uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2010\par 13:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in first zloty \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2000 float\par \par \uc2 * Govt says it fully supports move, shares c.bank concern\par \par \uc2 * Zloty falls 0.5 pct, but analysts say uptrend could resume\par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds analysts, MPC member, detail)\par \par \uc2 By Marcin Goettig and Dagmara Leszkowicz\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, April 9 (Reuters) - Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold zlotys on Friday, surprising markets with its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since introducing a free float in 2000 as it sought to temper the surging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's impact on exports and the wider economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement it had bought "some \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 " on the market around Friday. It gave no other details, but a Warsaw-based dealer said he believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about 40-50 million euros for zlotys.\par \par \uc2 The action, which the government said it backed fully, drove the zloty down 0.5 percent against the euro, though economists said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  might strengthen again.\par \par \uc2 The European Union's biggest ex-communist member, Poland is the only country in the bloc to have avoided recession last year and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors have taken note.\par \par \uc2 Before Friday's move, the zloty had gained 6 percent against the euro in the year so far and was near a 16-month high.\par \par \uc2 "This is a battle with our own success because the zloty's rise in the last three months is a result of the large demand for Polish bonds from abroad, as well as privatisation inflows," said Rafal Benecki, senior economist at ING Bank.\par \par \uc2 The country's robust growth prospects stand in stark contrast to a number of European countries, notably peripherals such as Greece or Spain.\par \par \uc2 Poland's debt levels are also well below the EU average, making Polish debt attractive to investors.\par \par \uc2 FINMIN STAMP OF APPROVAL\par \par \uc2 "This is definitely a beneficial move. It's a factor that the market needs to take into account in its analysis. We fully agree with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy on that matter," Deputy Finance Minister Dominik Radziwill told Reuters by telephone.\par \par \uc2 He said the ministry shared the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's concern over the zloty's strength.\par \par \uc2 At 1305 GMT, the zloty was at 3.8720/50 per euro, sharply weaker than 3.8340 earlier on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength has prompted concern that Poland could pay an economic price as zloty gains have made exports less competitive.\par \par \uc2 But some analysts doubt the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be able to halt the zloty's rise.\par \par \uc2 "We remain confident in the medium-term uptrend in the zloty," said Koon Chow, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . "We think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to slow the pace of zloty appreciation so as not to imperil the cautious cyclical recovery."\par \par \uc2 Chow said this kind of strategy was employed in other emerging market economies and there were good reasons for authorities not to try to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  too much either.\par \par \uc2 A bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness could stoke inflation and affect Poland's external debt position.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Kuba Jaworowksi and Pawel Sobczak, writing by Karolina Slowikowska; editing by John Stonestreet)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-ZLOTY/ (UPDATE 2, PIX, TV)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|PX|CZS|RDN|HX|BNX|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100409e649000t7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
