\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ UPDATE: Polish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Prepared For  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 528 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2010\par 16:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst comment, wraps in other zloty stories.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Marcin Sobczyk and Malgorzata Halaba \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared for an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent excessive strengthening of the zloty that could hamper economic growth, a management board member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "We're prepared technologically and psychologically for a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Witold Kozinski told a conference.\par \par \uc2 The zloty has been highly volatile over the past two years, reaching its strongest level ever at PLN3.20 against the euro in July 2008 and weakening dramatically during the global financial crisis to near its all-time weakest level of PLN4.92 against the euro in February 2009.\par \par \uc2 Over the past 14 months, the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has regained much of its pre-crisis strength. At 1321 GMT Thursday, it stood at PLN3.8519 to the euro.\par \par \uc2 Kozinski added that the zloty appears to be in a long-term upward trend, and warned that its rapid appreciation against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a negative impact on the economy and may impair the ability of Polish exporters to compete.\par \par \uc2 Polish government officials have also expressed concern that the strengthening of the zloty may have a negative impact on the country's economic recovery. Polish Economy Minister Waldemar Pawlak said Thursday that excessive zloty appreciation would "complicate the economic situation."\par \par \uc2 Pawlak also said the Polish Monetary Policy Council should keep key interest rates flat to curtail excessive growth of the zloty against core \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The growth forecast for this year is 3%, which is possible to achieve in a favorable environment," Pawlak said. "Because inflation is going down, there's no pressure to hike rates."\par \par \uc2 Poland's annual inflation rate fell to 2.6% in March from 2.9% in February, according to estimates released by the finance ministry.\par \par \uc2 Poland's key reference rate is at the historic low of 3.5%. Analysts expect that monetary tightening may take place later this year or be delayed until 2011.\par \par \uc2 MPC member Elzbieta Chojna-Duch said separately Thursday that the council will take the strength of the zloty compared with other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  into consideration when making interest rate decisions.\par \par \uc2 The MPC is watching the situation on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the stability of the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of its policy goals, she added.\par \par \uc2 Poland's annual inflation rate fell to 2.6% in March from 2.9% in February, according to estimates released by the finance ministry.\par \par \uc2 Poland's key reference rate is at the historic low of 3.5%. Analysts expect that monetary tightening may take place later this year or be delayed until 2011.\par \par \uc2 Citi economist Piotr Kalisz said Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on a much higher scale than the markets are anticipating, while the government is not expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but will no longer buy more euros on the market.\par \par \uc2 -By Malgorzata Halaba and Marcin Sobczyk, Dow Jones Newswires; +4822 447-2432;\par \par \uc2 marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 08, 2010 10:03 ET (14:03 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100408e648003pz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
