\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Polish  \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions \highlight\uc2  possible - cbanker\b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2010\par 17:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Combines with \b \highlight22\uc2 POLAND\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ZLOTY/, adds more detail)\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, April 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  may decide to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the zloty's appreciating trend proves to be long-term, a member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council (MPC) said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The zloty \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is near 16-month highs against the euro, though it was down some 0.5 percent on Thursday amid concerns over Greece's debt crisis. The 10-strong MPC can take a decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "If this trend proves long-term than we may start considering \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have a plan prepared for such a scenario," Anna Zielinska-Glebocka told TVN CNBC in an interview.\par \par \uc2 She also reiterated comments made on Wednesday that the zloty gains could prove temporary.\par \par \uc2 At 1557 GMT the euro traded at 3.8480 zlotys and despite Thursday's decline the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still 6.5 percent up from the beginning of 2010.\par \par \uc2 The deputy governor of the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Witold Kozinski, said on Thursday he believed the zloty was in a long-term appreciating trend. [nnWSF008896]\par \par \uc2 The zloty has become a hot topic in Poland, with some analysts saying further rises could jeopardise the country's still-fragile economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Some government officials have already expressed concerns that zloty gains are harming exports and fuelling imports.\par \par \uc2 Since the zloty became a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2000 no \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market have been conducted, but during a broad sell-off of emerging markets at the start of 2009 Prime Minister Donald Tusk suggested this could happen.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect Poland's economic growth to accelerate to 2.8 percent in 2010 from 1.7 percent in 2009.\par \par \uc2 The Paris-based Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD) said on Thursday it would probably revise upwards its 2010 growth forecast for Poland of 2.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 In a report, the OECD also said Poland's good economic fundamentals could trigger further zloty gains over the medium term as the country prepares for euro membership, noting that this could harm the competitiveness of Polish exports. (Reporting by Gabriela Baczynska and Kuba Jaworowski)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 POLAND\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ZLOTY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|PX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100408e64800154\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
