\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Polish Ctrl Bk's Filar: Can't Rule Out Rate "Optimal"\b0\par\par\uc2 184 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2009\par 09:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    WARSAW (Dow Jones)--Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monetary Policy Council member Dariusz Filar said Thursday he can't rule out that key interest rates are at their "optimal" level, given that there have been the first hopeful signals coming from economy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is quite possible the real economy has entered into a period of "gradual recovery," Filar told broadcaster Radio PiN.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Filar forecast Poland's first-quarter gross domestic product, or GDP, to post a 1.5% annual rise, while full-year annual GDP growth is likely to remain above zero, possibly at about 1%.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held key interest rates steady, the first pause in a six-month easing cycle to assess inflation and the stability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been under pressure.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark seven-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is 3.75%, the discount rate is 4%, the Lombard rate 5.25%, and the deposit rate 2.25%.\par \par \uc2 -By Malgorzata Halaba; Dow Jones Newswires, +4822 447 2430 6787; malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com [ 30-04-09 0732GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090430e54u000mq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
