\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ UPDATE: Poland's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Says May Act To Support Zloty\b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2009\par 17:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Adds further comment, background.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By David McQuaid \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council Wednesday supported government efforts to defend the zloty, explicitly reminding markets that direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets remains an option for the bank.\par \par \uc2 "The Monetary Policy Council is following a direct inflation-targeting strategy under a floating exchange-rate regime. Within this strategy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may deploy instruments directly influencing the zloty exchange rate," the rate-setting panel said in a statement after Wednesday's monthly rate meeting.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Wednesday, the 10-member MPC - presided over by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Slawomir Skrzypek but fully independent of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top management - decided to ease key interest rates 25 basis points, despite a 14.9% annual fall in January industrial output the council said confirms "a significant slowdown" is underway.\par \par \uc2 The cautious easing - less than the 50 basis points expected by economists only a week ago - followed sharp depreciation of the Polish zloty and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month, which prompted a coordinated verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday from the Czech, Hungarian, Polish, and Romanian central banks.\par \par \uc2 The zloty's plunge led Prime Minister Donald Tusk last week to warn his government would start selling euros to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , backed by the finance ministry's sale of euros Feb. 18, produced a 5% rebound in the zloty.\par \par \uc2 The MPC's reminder of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also served to correct an impression made by \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dovish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Slawomir Skrzypek, who several times in recent weeks has explicitly ruled out \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as costly and ineffective.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said such comments were a signal to investors betting against the zloty.\par \par \uc2 In its statement, the MPC retained language that it wants Poland to enter the European Union's ERM2 Exchange Rate Mechanism - a two-year \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  grid required of euro-zone applicants - "as soon as possible, after securing the necessary political backing for changes in the constitution and other laws needed for Poland to adopt the euro."\par \par \uc2 That at least partially meshes with government's fast-track plans to enter the euro zone by Jan. 1, 2012 - a timetable \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Skrzypek has said is too ambitious.\par \par \uc2 -By David McQuaid, Dow Jones Newswires; +4822 528-6776; david.mcquaid@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 25, 2009 11:40 ET (16:40 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020090820e52p0pdzb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
