\par\par \b \uc2 Poland - Factors to Watch on Feb 18\b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 2009\par 08:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 18 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Poland's financial markets on Wednesday. ALL TIMES GMT (Poland GMT + 1 hour):\par \par \uc2  ING LOSS\par \par \uc2 ING Bank Slaski\uc2  , a Polish unit of \uc2 ING Group\uc2  NV , swung to its first quarterly net loss in five years after writing down the value of its euro-denominated government bonds, it said on Wednesday. [ID:nWAR007927]\par \par \uc2  ERM-2 ENTRY\par \par \uc2  Poland is not ready for euro adoption at the moment and there are no economic reasons to enter the ERM-2 exchange mechanism this year, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head Slawomir Skrzypek was quoted as saying. [ID:nLI123980]\par \par \uc2  ZLOTY DIVES, PM \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's zloty dove to near an all time low on Tuesday, prompting the government to prop it up for the first time since it began a slide that has wiped out a third of its value and wreaked havoc among the corporate sector.[ID:LH310660]\par \par \uc2  NO BRE DIVIDEND\par \par \uc2  BRE Bank , the Polish unit of Germany's \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  , will propose no dividend payout from 2008 results because of the uncertainty on the financial markets, it said in a statement on Tuesday.[ID:nWAR007925]\par \par \uc2  PM SAYS 'NO' SCRAPPING OPTIONS\par \par \uc2  Poland's prime minister rejected a proposal by the junior coalition party on Tuesday to scrap toxic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options taken on by local companies only to see them pile on huge losses when when the zloty plunged.[ID:nLH539385]  \par \par \uc2  News editor of the day: Patryk Wasilewski\par \par \uc2  NOTE - For