\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Polish cbanker-may discuss  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  in Feb\b0\par\par\uc2 By Pawel Sobczak and Gabriela Baczynska   \par \uc2 624 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2009\par 11:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds prime minister's comments on the zloty in paras 5-6)\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Feb 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council (MPC) may discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at its meeting in February and decide whether such a move is warranted by the market situation, MPC member Dariusz Filar said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The zloty has shed 30 percent against the euro since touching an all-time high last July. It is down about 16 percent since just before the first interest rate cut of the current monetary easing cycle was made last November.\par \par \uc2 "The situation is such that the MPC must consider whether the current weakening of the zloty may be impacting inflation," Filar told Reuters. <EURPLN=> <PLN=>\par \par \uc2 "This does not mean that an (\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be carried out. It is too early to formulate an opinion that a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is needed or that it is not. We will be able to better answer this question at our February meeting."\par \par \uc2 Poland's Prime Minister, who recently said he did not see a need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, said on Friday the zloty weakening would not be long-lived as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should get support from the inflow of European Union (EU) funds.\par \par \uc2 EU's largest ex-communist member is entitled to 67 billion euros ($85.82 billion) from the bloc's 2007-2013 budget perspective.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in support of the zloty since the introduction of the free float regime nearly a decade ago, Filar noted. Poland's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves <PLCBFX=ECI> rose to 46.13 billion euros in January from 44.14 billion euros in December, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds reserves in U.S. dollars, euros and British pounds, but does not publish allocation details.\par \par \uc2 The MPC is set to hold its monthly meeting on Feb. 24-25.\par \par \uc2 Filar said monetary policy guidelines for 2009 allow for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help stabilise prices.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Slawomir Skrzypek, who this week ruled out \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said on Friday the weakening of the zloty was not caused by recent interest rate cuts.\par \par \uc2 When asked if the zloty had tumbled because of the monetary easing policy, Skrzypek told reporters: "There are completely different factors behind the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakening."\par \par \uc2 The governor also said he saw no impact of the zloty exchange rate on this year's inflation figure.\par \par \uc2 Analysts have said recently that the sharp zloty falls, mirroring other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses across the region as investors flee riskier emerging markets assets due to the global crisis, may spark inflationary risks and threaten the economy.\par \par \uc2 Some have signalled they are scaling back their interest rate cut expectations because of the zloty's depreciation.\par \par \uc2 "At a time of significant zloty weakening there is of course the question of whether it will affect inflation. If we decide that the exchange rate may be impacting future inflation, then this will limit scope for interest rate cuts in a decisive way," Filar said.\par \par \uc2 Concerns over sharp economic slowdown prompted the MPC to slash rates by a total of 175 basis points since November to 4.25 percent as the euro zone, Poland's main trade partner, headed into deep recession.\par \par \uc2 Underlining the deterioration in Poland's economy, a Labour Ministry source told Reuters on Friday unemployment likely rose to 10 percent last month from 9.5 percent in December. (Additional reporting by Maciej Onoszko, writing by Karolina Slowikowska and Dagmara Leszkowicz, Editing by Andy Bruce)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 POLAND\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 3, TV)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|PX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090206e526001ic\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
