\par\par \b \uc2 Poland - Factors to Watch on Feb 5\b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2009\par 08:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 5 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Poland's financial markets on Thursday. ALL TIMES GMT (Poland GMT + 1 hour):\par \par \uc2  RATES\par \par \uc2  The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council (MPC) should not cut interest rates in the coming months and any potential cuts should be on a limited scale, an MPC member was quoted as saying on Thursday by the daily Gazeta Wyborcza. [ID:nL5630054]\par \par \uc2  NEW DEPUTY FINANCE MINISTER?\par \par \uc2  Former CEO of energy group BOT Gornictwo i Energetyka Dominik Radziwill may become new deputy finance minister, daily Rzeczpospolita was quoted as saying, without giving sources.\par \par \uc2  ENEA\par \par \uc2  The power group ENEA had about 250 million zlotys of net profit in full-2008, the company's board member Slawomir Jankiewicz was quoted as saying on Thursday by daily Puls Biznesu\par \par \uc2  BOND ISSUES\par \par \uc2  Poland wants to place bonds denominated in Swiss francs and Japanese yen as soon as possible, Deputy Finance Minister Katarzyna Zajdel-Kurowska said on Wednesday, adding the ministry may also consdier selling bonds on the U.S. market. [ID:nL4486934]\par \par \uc2  ASSECO'S PROFITS\par \par \uc2  Eastern Europe's top software maker \uc2 Asseco Poland\uc2   expects 2008 net profit topping forecasts and further growth in 2009 as high-margin products help it weather the economic slowdown, its chief executive said. [ID:nL4728743] \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FX INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Wednesday he saw no need at present to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the zloty, which is touching its lowest levels since June 2004 as investors flee eastern Europe. [ID:nL4700334]\par \par \uc2  PKN AND LOTOS\par \par \uc2  Poland's two refiners, \uc2 PKN Orlen\uc2   and Lotos , swung deep into the red in 2008, tripped up by a sharp decline of the Polish zloty and charges related to the plunging value of their oil inventory. [ID:nL4438803]\par \par \uc2  News editor of the day: Dagmara Leszkowicz\par \par \uc2  NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming events see [PL/DIARY] and a calendar of east European economic indicators see [CONV/DIARY].\par \par \uc2    For other related news, double click on: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Polish equities       [PL-E]     E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  Polish money          [PL-M]     Polish debt           [PL-D]\par  Eastern Europe        [EEU]      All emerging markets  [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks            [HOT]      Stock markets         [STX]\par  Market debt news      [DBT]      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news            [FRX]\par  \par  For real-time index quotes, double click on:\par  Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20>  Budapest BUX <.BUX>  Prague PX <.PX>\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|PX|M|D|REVU|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090205e525000n7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
