\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Polish c.bank says no to  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  as zloty dives\b0\par\par\uc2 496 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2009\par 10:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (combines urgents, adds more cbanker quotes, other detail)\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Feb 4 (Reuters) - Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor on Wednesday said there was no need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the zloty, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dived to levels last seen in mid-2004, deepening worries over the EU's largest ex-communist economy. The zloty has slid another 5 percent against the euro in the last day, hit by a broad flight of investors out of eastern Europe that brought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's losses to 46 percent since it hit an all-time high last July.\par \par \uc2 Worries the economy could contract for the first time since the 1990s, and over how its foreign-owned banks will perform and lend in months ahead, have added to investors' aversion to risk in the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 But the zloty was weaker than the current levels before it joined the European Union in 2004 and Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and government have stuck to the policy of letting it float freely.\par \par \uc2 "It doesn't seem to be necessary to undertake \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market right now," Governor Slawomir Skrzypek told TVP Info in an interview on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 At 1005 GMT the zloty traded at 4.68 against the euro or 1.7 percent down from its Tuesday close.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Wednesday, Deputy Prime Minister and Economy Minister Waldemar Pawlak also said there was no need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "There is a question whether those \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be successful... Moreover, we need the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves we have, more than 55 billion euros, as collateral in case there is a necessity of entering ERM-2," Skrzypek said.\par \par \uc2 It could be "incredibly costly and incredibly risky" to enter the pre-euro Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM-2) right now, he added, citing some analysts who say Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves would not suffice to keep the zloty within the grid.\par \par \uc2 Referring to a government plan for almost 20 billion zlotys in budget savings announced on Tuesday, Skrzypek said it was important to maintain tight budget discipline at a time of slowdown.\par \par \uc2 "The government's push to do so (keep budget discipline) is correct," he said.\par \par \uc2 The centre-right government announced a savings plan amounting to 19.7 billion zlotys in 2009 budget spending.\par \par \uc2 It also vowed to keep the budget gap at the previously planned 18.2 billion zlotys even if 2009 growth slows to 1.7 percent, which Prime Minister Donald Tusk has said is its worst case scenario, from an expected 4.8 percent in 2008.\par \par \uc2 The budget had a surplus in January of 2.8-3.0 billion zlotys, Deputy Finance Minister Elzbieta Suchocka-Roguska told Reuters on Wednesday, adding she expected a deficit in the full January-February period. (Writing by Gabriela Baczynska and Kuba Jaworowski; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 POLAND\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|G|PX|BNX|RNP|DNP|PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090204e524000wr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
