\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Poland Ctrl Bk Gov: Growth Could Slow To 1% - 1.5% In 2009\b0\par\par\uc2 996 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2009\par 13:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 31 Jan 2009 07:45 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk: Ready To \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  On \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  But Don't See Need\par \par \uc2 31 Jan 2009 07:45 EDT *DJ  Poland Ctrl Bk Gov: Could Reduce Obligatory Reserves Ratio\par \par \uc2 31 Jan 2009 07:45 EDT *DJ  Poland Ctrl Bk Gov:Ready To Introduce Instruments If Needed\par \par \uc2 31 Jan 2009 07:45 EDT *DJ  Poland Ctrl Bk Gov: New Financial Instruments Not Needed Now\par \par \uc2 31 Jan 2009 07:45 EDT =DJ  DAVOS INTERVIEW:Poland Ctrl Bk:Rate Gap With ECB Significant\par \par \uc2 By Natasha Brereton\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 DAVOS, Switzerland (Dow Jones)--Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Slawomir Skrzypek says that risks to inflation are to the downside and called the difference in level between Polish and euro-zone interest rates remains significant.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Dow Jones Newswires at the World Economic Forum Friday, Skrzypek also said he doesn't expect Poland's economy to contract at all during the downturn and that there is "no chance" of a recession.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its key interest rate 75 basis points at its meeting earlier this week to 4.25%. The move followed a 75 basis point reduction in December. But that compares with interest rates of only 2% in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 "We are in a bias of easing the monetary policy. If you observe interest rates in Poland and in the euro zone, there is still a significant disparity," Skrzypek said, adding: "The decline in interest rates is likely to occur."\par \par \uc2 That reflects the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's expectation that there will be a "significant slowdown" in growth in 2009, to 1% to 1.5%, from around 5% last year and about 7% in 2007.\par \par \uc2 Despite that, Skrzypek is confident that gross domestic product growth would stay above zero, thanks to the well-diversified nature of Poland's economy.\par \par \uc2 "In Poland, I think there's no chance of recession," Skrzypek said. "There's no fear of recession."\par \par \uc2 Inflation could fall below the bank's target of 2.5% "in the next quarters," he said, but he declined to discuss the bank's new forecasts it will publish in February.\par \par \uc2 While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it has done everything it needs to do to join the euro, financial turmoil could make concluding the process more tricky.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Poland's finance minister was reported saying that plans to enter the European Union's ERM2 exchange rate mechanism in mid-2009 and adopt the euro on Jan. 1, 2012 could be delayed if instability persists in global markets.\par \par \uc2 The E.U.'s Maastricht Treaty requires euro-zone candidate countries to fix their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the euro within ERM2's plus/minus 15% trading band for a minimum of two years before receiving clearance to adopt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "In normal times, volatility of our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was about 5%-to-6%. Now its average is 20% but there was a time when it was even 35%," Skrzypek said. "It's not a favorable time to join the exchange rate mechanism."\par \par \uc2 He noted that it was very hard to predict financial market conditions even a month ahead at the moment.\par \par \uc2 Skrzypek said he believed the zloty's current value was "below fundamentals," reflecting the flight-to-safe-haven trend and nervousness surrounding the region. Poland's economy has been relatively resilient during the downturn, but the plight of some of its emerging European neighbors has fueled concerns about the area as a whole.\par \par \uc2 "I'm not worried about the current exchange rate now. Maybe the market judged us unfairly but it also creates a favorable situation for our exports," Skrzypek said.\par \par \uc2 While there has been increasing discussion of the potential for governments to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adjust their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' values to more rational levels, the governor was confident that the zloty would return to fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, he indicated the government was ready to take action if it believed that to be necessary.\par \par \uc2 "We are ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but I think such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not needed," Skrzypek said.\par \par \uc2 "I think the flexibility of the economy and all the positive factors will in a natural way help our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to come back to fundamentals."\par \par \uc2 Turning to the financial markets, Skrzypek said that although Poland's market was actually overliquid from a macro perspective, tensions could emerge on a micro basis between financial institutions.\par \par \uc2 Skrzypek said the bank is exploring introducing new instruments based on the experiences of the U.S. Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "At the moment, it's not required but we are prepared," he said.\par \par \uc2 The governor said another option is to increase the frequency of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  providing funding in zlotys and euros.\par \par \uc2 It's also considering whether to lower its mandatory reserve rate, which stands at 3.5%, above the ECB's 2%.\par \par \uc2 "We are carefully monitoring the market and we are ready to introduce the next measures when they are needed. Reaching this level (2%) in a few steps could be the best strategy," Skrzypek said.\par \par \uc2 Summit Web site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.weforum.org/en/index.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.weforum.org/en/index.htm  }}}\par \par \uc2 -By Natasha Brereton, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 20 7842 9254; natasha.brereton@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 31 Jan 2009 07:55 EDT *DJ  Poland Ctrl Bk Gov: CPI Could Fall Below 2.5% Goal This Yr\par \par \uc2 31 Jan 2009 07:55 EDT *DJ  Poland Ctrl Bk Gov: Not Favorable \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Situation To Join ERM\par \par \uc2 31 Jan 2009 07:55 EDT *DJ  Poland Ctrl Bk: See GDP Growth Above Zero During Downturn\par \par \uc2 31 Jan 2009 07:55 EDT *DJ  Poland Ctrl Bk Gov: See "No Chance" Of Economic Recession\par \par \uc2 31 Jan 2009 07:55 EDT *DJ  Poland Ctrl Bk Gov:Risks To Downside, In Policy Easing Bias\par \par \uc2 31 Jan 2009 07:56 EDT *DJ  Poland Ctrl Bk Gov: Rate Gap With Euro-Zone Significant\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 31, 2009 07:56 ET (12:56 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020090819e51v0phv2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
