\par\par \b \uc2 Poland - Factors to Watch on Jan 6\b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2009\par 08:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Jan 6 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Poland's financial markets on Tuesday. ALL TIMES GMT (Poland GMT + 1 hour):\par \par \uc2 RUSSIAN GAS\par \par \uc2 Poland does not need to start limiting gas supplies yet despite a fall in gas deliveries because of a dispute between Russia and Ukraine, an energy advisor to the prime minister said in a radio interview.\par \par \uc2 Michal Wozniak added Poland would not be forced to undertake any extraordinary steps for at least three weeks.\par \par \uc2 PKO, PEKAO\par \par \uc2 Polish banks may run out of cash for loans and authorities should take urgent steps to prevent the crunch from dampening economic growth, the heads of Poland's two largest banks, Pekao and PKO BP , wrote in a joint newspaper article.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the Polish zloty weakens significantly although such a move is not currently needed, a deputy governor said. [ID:nWAR007748]\par \par \uc2 EURO\par \par \uc2 Poland should not decide in a referendum whether to adopt the euro as the global financial crisis may weaken support for the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  among Poles, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Andrzej Wojtyna tells Rzeczpospolita. [ID:nL6415202]\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MEETS ECONOMISTS\par \par \uc2 Polish President Lech Kaczynski is set to meet with economists and financial experts to discuss tha economic situation at 1100 GMT.\par \par \uc2 GAS SUPPLIES\par \par \uc2 Gas deliveries to Poland via Ukraine remained lower by 5 million cubic metres daily on Monday, but were recompensated by imports through Belarus, Poland's gas monopoly \uc2 PGNiG\uc2  said in a statement. [ID:nL5253824]\par \par \uc2 ENERGY PRICES RISING\par \par \uc2 Poland's energy market regulator URE approved an average 10 percent rise in wholesale energy prices for 12 out of 14 energy trading companies. [ID:nL5198810]\par \par \uc2 C.BANKERS SPLIT\par \par \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymakers on Monday offered differing views on the scale of the economic slowdown in 2009, underscoring uncertainty about the impact of the global financial crisis on the EU's largest eastern member.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nL537543]\par \par \uc2 TVN\par \par \uc2 The national audience share of TVN, flagship channel of Poland's largest listed media group TVN , fell to 15.3 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in December from 16.2 a year earlier.     [ID:nL528461]\par    \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 News editor of the day: Gabriela Baczynska, + 48 22 653 97 22\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming events see [PL/DIARY] and a calendar of east European economic indicators see [CONV/DIARY].\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For other related news, double click on: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Polish equities       [PL-E]     E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  Polish money          [PL-M]     Polish debt           [PL-D]\par  Eastern Europe        [EEU]      All emerging markets  [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks            [HOT]      Stock markets         [STX]\par  Market debt news      [DBT]      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news            [FRX]\par  \par  For real-time index quotes, double click on:\par  Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20>  Budapest BUX <.BUX>  Prague PX <.PX>\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|PX|M|D|REVU|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090106e516000de\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppic