\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 1- \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  weaken, Poland's zloty at 2-1/2 year low\b0\par\par\uc2 639 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2008\par 10:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Dec 18 (Reuters) - Emerging Europe's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened further on Thursday, with the Polish zloty at a 2-1/2 year-low and the Czech crown near its lowest level this year as risks to economic growth build.\par \par \uc2 Data in the region has drawn a darker picture of its economies and the countries' central banks have moved to cut rates, while appetite for emerging assets has waned.\par \par \uc2 The Czech crown <EURCZK=> opened lower Thursday, a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut the main repo rate to 2.25 percent, its lowest level since July and hinted at more cuts as the economic crisis gathers pace. [ID:nLH141377]\par \par \uc2 "Fundamentally the story is the same; the global slowdown is here and there is nothing to hedge (against)," a local Prague-based dealer said.\par \par \uc2 Data on Thursday showed Czech retail sales unexpectedly dipped in October, prompting some analysts to warn the slowdown in production was starting to hit consumer behaviour harder. [ID:nLI114058]\par \par \uc2 In Poland, the zloty <EURPLN=> fell slightly to a 2 1/2 year low in early trade, and dealers said prospects for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are negative.\par \par \uc2 "I expect the zloty will reach the level of 4.20 to the euro quickly as risk aversion in the region grows and domestically we have this ongoing options problem," said Jan Koprowski, dealer at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in Warsaw.\par \par \uc2 The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost more than 24 percent since the summer when it was at its all-time high to the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the reversal has hit some companies that bet wrongly on further appreciation in the zloty. [ID:nLH476303]\par \par \uc2 Also on Thursday, Poland's stats office releases industrial output and producer prices data for November and analysts expect output to have fallen as much as 5.1 percent year-on-year.\par \par \uc2 Romania's leu <EURRON=> was down 0.2 percent in quiet trade, but the regional economic gloom and political uncertainty are seen weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  further.\par \par \uc2 "Foreign players are buying euros, betting on a recoupling of the leu with the region and especially with the zloty," one dealer said. "It has every reason to do this as Romania has weaker fundamentals than \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 "But they still fear \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so the recoupling takes some time. Apparently, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not want the leu to depreciate sharply, but gradually."\par \par \uc2 The Democrat-Liberals and Social Democrats, who have forged a governing coalition, are expected to announce the names of the future ministers. [ID:nLH159546]\par \par \uc2 The parliament is expected to endorse the cabinet on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ----------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT-------------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                   close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                            change   change\par                                            today    in 2008 \par Czech crown      <EURCZK=>   26.41    26.263  -0.56%   +0.33%\par Polish zloty     <EURPLN=>    4.108    4.106  -0.05%   -14.1%\par Hungarian forint <EURHUF=>  265.59   265.33   -0.1%    -5.04%\par Croatian kuna    <EURH