\par\par \b \uc2 Poland - Factors to Watch on Oct 27\b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2008\par 08:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Oct 27 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Poland's financial markets on Mondayday. ALL TIMES GMT (Poland GMT + 1 hour):\par \par \uc2 PM MEETS THE MAIN OPPOSITION PARTY LEADER\par \par \uc2 Polish Prime Minister Donald Tusk meets the main opposition party Law and Justice (PiS) leader Jaroslaw Kaczynski to discuss the current economic situation. (1500).\par \par \uc2 PAK\par \par \uc2 Poland considers selling its 50 percent stake of electricity provider \uc2 Patnow-Adamow-Konin\uc2  (PAK) to a sector investor, the Treasury Minister Aleksander Grad tells Gazeta Prawna.\par \par \uc2 TENDER\par \par \uc2 Poland's finance ministry will offer 1.0 billion zlotys in 13-week treasury bills at Monday tender.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNMENT HELP FOR BANKS\par \par \uc2 The Polish government plans to shortly introduce several measures to help its banks weather the global financial turmoil, including state guarantees and loans, according to the draft of a bill seen by Reuters on Sunday. [Id:nLQ107442]\par \par \uc2 ZLOTY REBOUND\par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Friday the zloty may rebound soon from its sharp losses because the economy's fundamentals are sound, and he also said he did not foresee the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to calm volatility. [ID:nLO201754]\par \par \uc2 PGNiG\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gas monopoly \uc2 PGNiG\uc2  said on Friday its third-quarter net profit forecast of 172 million zlotys ($56 million) was "realistic".\par \par \uc2 ENEA\par \par \uc2 Czech energy producer CEZ may take part in the flotation of power producer and distributor Enea, the head of CEZ's Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday. [ID:nLO736386]\par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Dagmara Leszkowicz\par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming events see [PL/DIARY] and a calendar of east European economic indicators see [CONV/DIARY].\par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Polish equities       [PL-E]     E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  Polish money          [PL-M]     Polish debt           [PL-D]\par  Eastern Europe        [EEU]      All emerging markets  [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks            [HOT]      Stock markets         [STX]\par  Market debt news      [DBT]      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news            [FRX]\par  \par  For real-time index quotes, double click on:\par  Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20>  Budapest BUX <.BUX>  Prague PX <.PX>\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|REVU|E|RBN|PX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081027e4ar000nt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
