\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2  won't  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to weaken zloty-deputy min\b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2008\par 13:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds background, detail)\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, July 9 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not plan to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the zloty <EURPLN=>, which has hit record highs against the euro in recent days, Deputy Finance Minister Katarzyna Zajdel-Kurowska said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "There will be no \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It is not the government's intention to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Zajdel-Kurowska told reporters.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not the government, would have to conduct any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and is an independent institution.\par \par \uc2 The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reached a fresh all-time high against the euro on Wednesday, touching 3.2550 in one transaction. It has gained 31.5 percent against the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Poland joined the European Union in 2004.\par \par \uc2 Economists say the zloty's sharp appreciation could dent Poland's robust economic growth, especially exports, although it is also helping the fight against resurgent inflation and may reduce the need for further interest rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 A member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council, Member (MPC) Miroslaw Pietrewicz, told Reuters on Tuesday that if the zloty appreciated further it could cause economic growth to fall below 4 percent in the fourth quarter, well below the 6.1 percent posted in the first quarter. Last weekend, MPC member Halina Wasilewska-Trenkner urged against any Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying in a newspaper interview that they were costly and failed to bring the desired effects. (Reporting by Marcin Goettig, writing by Dagmara Leszkowicz and Gareth Jones; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-ZLOTY/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|PX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080709e479001t7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
