\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Speculators to drive zloty up before euro-minister\b0\par\par\uc2 By Marcin Grajewski   \par \uc2 528 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2008\par 17:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with details, background)\par \par \uc2 BRUSSELS, July 8 (Reuters) - Poland's zloty \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <EURPLN=> is likely to face strong appreciation pressure in the pre-euro ERM-2 exchange rate system, as was the case with the Slovak crown, the Polish finance minister said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Jacek Rostowski told a news conference such pressure might require costly \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so the government would analyse preventative options.\par \par \uc2 "Slovakia ... is joining the euro zone after a significant \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation so we can suspect that a well-prepared country like Poland may be subject to strong speculation towards appreciation on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," he said.\par \par \uc2 "This may create problems, so we will analyse this case (Slovakia), ponder what is the best way to prevent this."\par \par \uc2 Rostowski was speaking after Slovakia cleared the final hurdle towards joining the euro zone on Jan. 1, 2009. EU finance ministers set the rate at which the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will replace its crown <EURSKK=> -- at 30.1260 crowns to the euro.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts believe Poland could join the ERM-2, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability test for joining the euro, in 2009 at the earliest and adopt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2012.\par \par \uc2 The Slovak crown has gained some 22 percent against the euro since July 2006, when the current left-wing government took over. Slovakia has twice revalued the central parity rate in the ERM-2, around which the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of a euro candidate is allowed to fluctuate within a narrow band.\par \par \uc2 Poland's zloty is expected to face similar pressure in the ERM-2, so the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may need to conduct costly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the zloty within the required band, Rostowski said.\par \par \uc2 "What happened in Slovakia may encourage players in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to expect appreciation (in \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), which may mean a need for sizeable \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid this."\par \par \uc2 Under \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current free-float system, the zloty has gained 8.5 percent against the euro since the start of the year and more than 31 percent since Poland joined the EU in 2004.\par \par \uc2 The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a record high of 3.2990 against the euro on Tuesday after breaking through the key psychological level of 3.3 zlotys.\par \par \uc2 Rostowski also said the EU's go-ahead for Slovakia to join the euro zone despite ECB doubts over the country's inflation was a good signal for Poland's euro bid.\par \par \uc2 "There were certain temptations to sharpen (euro entry) criteria for Slovakia ..., attempts to look for excuses not to accept Slovakia," he said.\par \par \uc2 "The fact those temptations were rejected is a positive result from the point of view of Poland's future membership of the euro," he added.\par \par \uc2 The ECB had doubts over whether Slovakia met the euro entry inflation criterion in a sustainable way, but the European Commission, the EU's executive arm, finally decided to recommend that the country be allowed to enter the euro zone. (Editing by Dale Hudson)\par \par \uc2 POLAND-EURO/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|PX|CZS|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080708e4780017t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
