\par\par \b \uc2 Poland - Factors to Watch on July 7\b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2008\par 08:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, July 7 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Poland's financial markets on Monday. ALL TIMES GMT (Poland GMT + 2 hours):\par \par \uc2 WARSAW LISTINGS\par \par \uc2 Polish parliament will soon start works on a bill to make it easier for foreign companies to list on the Warsaw bourse, a move that could encourage IPOs of Ukrainian and Belarussian on the Polish market, writes Parkiet.\par \par \uc2 ZLOTY\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the soaring zloty <EURPLN=>, which has reached new all-time highs against the euro this week, a Monetary Policy Council member Halina Wasilewska-Trenkner tells Parkiet. [ID:nL05415320]\par \par \uc2 SHIPYARDS\par \par \uc2 The European Commission has given Poland a preliminary blessing to privatise its shipyards, a move that could save the birthplace of the anti-Communist Solidarity movement from bankruptcy, local media reported on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for the Brussels-based Commission, the European Union's top competition regulator, said no decision had been taken. [ID:nL05493459]\par \par \uc2 POLIMEX-MOSTOSTAL\par \par \uc2 Polish builder Polimex raised sales by 20-30 percent in the first half, as it continues to benefit from a wide variety of construction projects in the developing economy, its chief executive tells Reuters. [ID:nL04117612]\par \par \uc2 News editor of the day:Dagmara Leszkowicz\par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming events see [PL/DIARY] and a calendar of east European economic indicators see [CONV/DIARY].\par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on: \par \