\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Poland has room for one more hike-MPC's Wojtyna\b0\par\par\uc2 483 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 2008\par 08:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds MPC member Wasilewska-Trenkner on \b \highlight22\uc2 fx interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, May 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  has room for more monetary policy tightening soon but it should be limited to one interest rate hike, Monetary Policy Council (MPC) member Andrzej Wojtyna was quoted as saying on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "There is still room for some monetary policy tightening soon," Wojtyna told Rzeczpospolita daily in an interview. "But, like some of my colleagues at the (Monetary Policy) Council, I think it is rather one hike, than two."\par \par \uc2  Wojtyna added that April would have been a good time for a rate increase and that it would make little difference now if the next hike came in May or June.\par \par \uc2  The MPC has raised its main interest rate seven times since April 2007 to the current level of 5.75 percent to fight accelerating inflation, but left them on hold last month.\par \par \uc2  The 10-member council is due to meet again on rates next week and is expected to keep them unchanged again.\par \par \uc2  Though inflation slightly eased in April to 4.0 percent from 4.1 percent for March, it is expected to pick up again later in the year.\par \par \uc2  Another MPC member, Halina Wasilewska-Trenkner, told Radio PiN the strong zloty, flirting with an all-time high and some 30 percent up against the euro since Poland joined the EU in 2004, also helped to curb the need for monetary tightening.\par \par \uc2  For example, the zloty has capped price growth of imported fuel, she said. Asked about the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the zloty and help relieve pressure on Polish exporters, she said this would be a bad idea.\par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Polish conditions, given today's situation on the global financial markets, are dangerous and would bring no result," Wasilewska-Trenkner said.\par \par \uc2  EURO DATE\par \par \uc2  Wojtyna also reiterated his view that setting a date to join the euro zone would create incentives for economic reform. \par \par \uc2  "The date factor plays a significant role," Wojtyna said. "We have quite a strange situation now. The declarations of the finance ministry and the government are not clear, especially when it comes to the date."\par \par \uc2  "It is said that problems, if they occur, will occur on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and inflationary criteria side and also it may be difficult meeting the budget criteria if a more serious economic slowdown happens." \par \par \uc2  Government officials say Poland, the European Union's biggest ex-communist economy, could join the pre-euro mechanism ERM2 in 2009. This could indicate joining the euro zone in 2011 or 2012, but no official dates have been fixed. \par \par \uc2  The MPC has said in the past it supported euro adoption as soon as possible.   (Writing by Gabriela Baczynska, editing by Gareth Jones and Gerrard Raven)    \par \par \uc2 POLAND-RATES/WOJTYNA (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|PX|BNX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080519e45j000bx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
