\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-INTERVIEW-Polish PM says euro in 2012 probable   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Pawel Florkiewicz and Gabriela Baczynska   \par \uc2 639 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 13:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Releads, adds quotes, more detail)   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, March 6 (Reuters) - Poland will probably adopt the euro in 2012 if the government can ensure the move will benefit as many Poles as possible, including those who are not well-off, Prime Minister Donald Tusk said on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Hopes of quicker euro adoption were one of the main reasons behind markets' warm welcome of the election victory of Tusk's centre-right Civic Platform last year, which ran a campaign promising the euro, lower taxes and less red tape.   \par \par \uc2 Tusk's government, in office for just over 100 days, has so far refused to set a formal entry date, however.   \par \par \uc2 He said this was because of uncertainties related to the global economic outlook and insisted the government was working to make euro entry possible.   \par \par \uc2 "2012 is quite probable. We will do it quickly and efficiently, but we are not going to set a specific target date. I prefer to make promises that I can keep," Tusk told Reuters in an interview.   \par \par \uc2 Tusk said, however, that adopting the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may harm the financial standing of Poles, still way behind in the race to catch up with their richer Western counterparts nearly 20 years after the fall of communism in 1989.   \par \par \uc2 "Poland in no way can be compared to any country that is already in the euro zone ... I am talking about millions of Poles that live on the verge of the social minimum ... The number of people who are not well-to-do is incomparably bigger," Tusk said.   \par \par \uc2 "We cannot ignore the social problem. We want to enter the euro as quickly as possible but not for the price that large group of Poles would have to pay," Tusk added, pointing to the possible growth of inflation following euro entry as his main concern.   \par \par \uc2 Tusk played down concerns, however, that the government became cool on the euro after the election victory.   \par \par \uc2 "Nobody needs to convince me, finance minister (Jacek) Rostowski, other ministers, to undertake action that requires courage, that requires a risk, also in the face of public opinion," he said.   \par \par \uc2 "(We will enter) when we reach the status of a country that meets all the requirements."   \par \par \uc2 C.BANK CONTROVERSY   \par \par \uc2 Tusk said he would not approve one of two candidates for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor, Witold Kozinski, due to his controversial views on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Kozinski, an ex-central banker, was nominated to join the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board by the bank's governor Slawomir Skrzypek earlier this year. He spooked markets by suggesting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be used to tame the vibrant zloty.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had a free float for almost a decade.   \par \par \uc2 "I cannot take responsibility regarding Mr. Kozinski," Tusk said.   \par \par \uc2 He said he would approve the other candidate to the board, commercial banker Piotr Wiesiolek.   \par \par \uc2 Tusk's comments spurred an immediate reaction from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which said it would not withdraw Kozinski's nomination, signalling a deepening of the row between the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The row at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  erupted when two of Skrzypek's deputies resigned at the start of the year. One accused the governor of mismanaging the bank and pressing the bank's economists to massage down inflation forecasts.   \par \par \uc2 When Skrzypek, a political appointee of the previous conservative administration, took the job in January 2007, analysts said he lacked credentials for the job.   \par \par \uc2 Tusk said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to be in a crisis.   \par \par \uc2 "I am a fanatic supporter of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independence but I am aware that (before Skrzypek) we have never had a political leadership at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. (Writing by Karolina Slowikowska)   \par \par \uc2 POLAND-EURO/ (UPDATE 2, INTERVIEW, PX, TV)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|PX|G|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080306e436000y7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
