\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-Poland needs caution on euro -econ minister   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Adam Jasser and Gabriela Baczynska   \par \uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2008\par 17:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Jan 10 (Reuters) - Current volatility in global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is complicating Poland's preparations to join the euro zone, Economy Minister Waldemar Pawlak said on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Pawlak said Poland needed time to determine the right exchange rate at which to propose pegging the zloty to the euro to be able to keep it stable for two years inside a special fluctuation band for euro candidate nations, the ERM-2.   \par \par \uc2 "At the moment, I think we need to think this over again," Pawlak said in an interview.   \par \par \uc2 He said the risk of getting the peg wrong and the level of global uncertainty was such that discussions about the euro exchange rate or the timing of ERM entry were theoretical at this stage.   \par \par \uc2 "In my opinion...the two-year period of staying in the corridor, with the current dynamic of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, looks like a theoretical not a practical solution," he said.   \par \par \uc2 "The time spent in the corridor sometimes costs serious \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and creates a huge temptation for serious market speculation."   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's centre-right government, which took power in November last year, says it wants to adopt the euro in principle but only when the move will not disturb the economy and when it puts public finances in good order.   \par \par \uc2 It said entry before the current parliament's term expires in 2011 is unlikely.   \par \par \uc2 Any euro zone candidate needs to stay in the ERM 2 for two years, meaning Poland should consider pegging the zloty next year or in 2010 to replace zlotys with euros in 2012.   \par \par \uc2 The largest ex-communist economy in the EU hopes to cut the budget gap to below 3 percent of GDP this year and convince the European Commission to remove it from the blacklist of budgetary offenders, the biggest obstacle to euro entry.   \par \par \uc2 But rising inflation and the strengthening zloty, which rose 6 percent versus the euro and 14 percent against the dollar last year, have created a new headache for both government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymakers.   \par \par \uc2 Pawlak said the zloty's strength is approaching the limits of what is justified by economic fundamentals.   \par \par \uc2 He acknowledged that entering the ERM-2 sooner rather than later could help provide an anchor to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and provide relief to exporters but said he was concerned whether Poland would be able to defend the level from any speculative attack.   \par \par \uc2 "I think the exchange rate at which to enter is the key issue," he said, adding that inter-government discussions on the euro peg would be strictly confidential.   \par \par \uc2 Pawlak acknowledged the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had little means to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising further on the back of the strong economy.   \par \par \uc2 "This is largely in the hands of the market and global experience teaches us that direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are very costly and one should keep at arm's length from them," he said.   \par \par \uc2 He said, however, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is expected to hike interest rates in response to rising inflation, should consider the impact of monetary tightening on the zloty.   \par \par \uc2 "High interest rates tend to help a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate by making investments (into money instruments and bonds) more profitable," he said. (Writing by Adam Jasser; editing by Tony Austin)   \par \par \uc2 POLAND-ZLOTY (INTERVIEW, PICTURE, TV)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|PX|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080110e41a001n6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
