\par\par \b \uc2 Polish zloty weaker after Slovak  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 16:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, March 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's zloty fell on Tuesday alongside other central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Slovakia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the rise of the Slovak crown.  \par \par \uc2 The zloty fell in the morning around 0.4 percent. It recovered about half those losses in the afternoon and gained a foothold around 3.8730 to the euro.  \par \par \uc2 "The zloty has now calmed," said Marcin Zoltaniecki, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Raiffeisen Bank in Warsaw. "The zloty didn't move out of a range of 3.86-3.88 to the euro and there's no reason to think that will change this week."  \par \par \uc2 Bond yields held steady ahead of an auction on Wednesday of 1.8 billion zlotys ($617.1 million) of five-year bonds that the finance ministry is expected to easily place.  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak crown rose three percent on Monday after the revaluation of its euro peg in the ERM-2 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  grid, prompting the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) to sell crowns on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. -------------- MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1520 GMT---------------------- EUR/PLN <EURPLN=> 3.8721 vs 3.8646 early on Tuesday USD/PLN <PLN=> 2.9131 vs 2.9043 2-yr bond yield (OK1208)<0#PL104360=> 4.53 pct vs. 4.52 pct 5-yr bond yield (PS0412)<0#PL104659=> 4.98 pct vs. 4.99 pct 10-yr bond yield (DS1017)<0#PL104543=> 5.18 pct vs. 5.19 pct ---------------------------------------------------------------  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ZLOTY-AFTERNOON|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M