\par\par \b \uc2 Poland - Factors to Watch on Nov 17  \b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2006\par 08:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Nov 17 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Poland's financial markets on Friday. ALL TIMES GMT (Poland GMT + 1 hour):  \par \par \uc2 BUDGET ROW  \par \par \uc2 Poland's Finance Minister Zyta Gilowska has dismissed European Commission criticism of Warsaw's budget plans and accused it of taking a tougher line on Poland than other EU members. [ID:nWAR005010]  \par \par \uc2 PKN CHIEF RUMOURS  \par \par \uc2 Speaking on radio TOK FM, former Prime Minister Kazimierz Marcinkiewicz played down rumours, but did not rule out, that he was being considered as a replacement for oil group PKN Orlen's chief executive Igor Chalupec.  \par \par \uc2 PEKAO MERGER  \par \par \uc2 Poland's Bank Pekao said on Thursday its market value should rise to 14.7 billion euros ($18.83 billion) when it absorbs Bank BPH , making it the biggest listed Polish company. [ID:nL16831916]  \par \par \uc2 Business daily Parkiet reports France's largest retail bank Credit Agricole is interested in bidding for the 200 BPH branches and other assets that Pekao will sell as part of the deal.  \par \par \uc2 Belgium's KBC , Polish financial group Getin and Britain's largest bank HSBC have also previously been raised as potential buyers.  \par \par \uc2 RATES  \par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should keep interest rates on hold for several quarters to come as inflation remains low capped by the strong zloty and productivity gains, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate-setting official said on Thursday. [ID:nL16632069]  \par \par \uc2 WAGES  \par \par \uc2 Average gross wages in Poland's corporate sector rose 4.7 percent year-on-year <PLWAGE=ECI> in October, a touch faster than market expectations, statistical office data showed on Thursday. [ID:nL16926868]  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 POLAND\b0 \highlight\uc2 -RUSSIA ROW  \par \par \uc2 European Union president Finland \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday to try to break a deadlock between \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Russia that threatens to block the launch of landmark talks on an EU-Russia strategic partnership next week. [ID:nL16871141]  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Patrick Graham  \par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming events see [PL/DIARY] and a calendar of east European economic indicators see [CONV/DIARY].  \par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on:   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Polish equities       [PL-E]     E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  Polish money          [PL-M]     Polish debt           [PL-D]\par  Eastern Europe        [EEU]      All emerging markets  [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks            [HOT]      Stock markets         [STX]\par  Market debt news      [DBT]      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news            [FRX]\par  \par  For real-time index quotes, double click on:\par  Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20>  Budapest BUX <.BUX>  Prague PX <.PX>\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Poland - Factors to Watch on Nov 17|LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|PX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061117e2bh0011j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
