\par\par \b \uc2 Poland - Factors to Watch on Sept 12  \b0\par\par\uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2006\par 08:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Sept 12 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Poland's financial markets on Tuesday. ALL TIMES GMT (Poland GMT + 2 hours):  \par \par \uc2 LOCAL ELECTIONS  \par \par \uc2 Poland will hold local elections on Nov 12, Prime Minister Jaroslaw Kaczynski said during a televised address to the nation on Monday. [ID:nL11638181]  \par \par \uc2 FOREIGN DEBT ISSUES  \par \par \uc2 Poland will issue its first foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds in almost a year in October or November, likely followed by a benchmark euro bond issue in January of next year, a deputy finance ministry said on Monday. [ID:nL11623941]  \par \par \uc2 RATES SEEN UP IN Q1  \par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to up interest rates for the first time in over two years in the first quarter of 2007 due to signs inflation may climb faster than earlier thought, a Reuters poll showed on Monday. [ID:nL11649799]  \par \par \uc2 PGNIG NEW CEO  \par \par \uc2 Polish state-owned natural gas group PGNiG on Monday appointed supervisory board chairman Krzysztof Glogowski its new chief executive. [ID:nL11207961]  \par \par \uc2 PKN SUPERVISORY BOARD MEETS  \par \par \uc2 Polish top oil group PKN Orlen's supervisory board may decide on Tuesday to add a new member to the company's management, reports daily Gazeta Prawna. It says chief executive Igor Chalupec will likely remain in his post.  \par \par \uc2 PRIME MINISTER IN U.S.  \par \par \uc2 Poland's Prime Minister Jaroslaw Kaczynski leaves for the United States late on Tuesday. His four-day visit is due to focus on energy security and defence.  \par \par \uc2 GRAIN \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  SALES  \par \par \uc2 The European Commission may soon agree to allow \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell 200,000 tonnes of milling wheat from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stocks to local millers in order to prevent prices from rising further, reports daily Rzeczpospolita.  \par \par \uc2 CEDC WANTS TO DEBUT ON WARSAW BOURSE  \par \par \uc2 Central European Distribution Corporation (CEDC), the biggest producer and distributor of alcohol in Poland, wants to enter the Warsaw bourse, writes daily Puls Biznesu. It quotes CEDC's chief executive as saying CEDC may finalise its preparations for the initial public offering this year.  \par \par \uc2 BIOFUELS REGULATION  \par \par \uc2 Poland's Economy Minister Piotr Wozniak on Monday signed a regulation on biofuels that paves the way for local producers to sell diesel fuel including 20 percent of esters from vegetable matter, writes daily Rzeczpospolita. It says the finance ministry is expected to decide on the excise tax on biofuels this month.  \par \par \uc2 NEW BANKING LAW  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 treasury ministry\b0 \highlight\uc2  is preparing a new banking law which would allow banks to split, writes daily Parkiet. New regulations are necessary after Italian UniCredito merged with Polish Bank BPH and is now obliged to sell some branches.  \par \par \uc2 POLKOMTEL EYES FIXED-LINE SERVICES  \par \par \uc2 Polish mobile operator Polkomtel may move into fixed-line telecommunication, writes daily Parkiet. The group's chief executive was quoted as saying that he was analysing possible co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  or capital investments with fixed-line operator Telefonia Dialog and other companies.  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Ewa Krukowska; Reuters Messaging: ewa.krukowska.reuters.com@reuters.net; tel. +48 22 6539710  \par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming events see [PL/DIARY] and a calendar of east European economic indicators see [CONV/DIARY].  \par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on:   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Polish equities       [PL-E]     E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  Polish money          [PL-M]     Polish debt           [PL-D]\par  Eastern Europe        [EEU]      All emerging markets  [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks            [HOT]      Stock markets         [STX]\par  Market debt news      [DBT]      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news            [FRX]\par  \par  For real-time index quotes, double click on:\par  Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20>  Budapest BUX <.BUX>  Prague PX <.PX>\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|PX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060912e29c000bi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
