\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-Polish c.bank won't  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to steady zloty-banker  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Marcin Goclowski  \par \uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2006\par 18:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Jan 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government should stop buying zlotys on the market if it wants a weaker zloty, and cannot count on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  or deep rate cuts to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a central banker said on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "If the ministry returned to its previous debt managagement strategy it would help stabilise the exchange rate," Dariusz Filar, a member of the bank's 10-strong monetary policy council, told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market are not likely," he added.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly criticised the finance ministry's strategy of increasing foreign borrowing and swapping part of the proceeds for zlotys on the interbank market. Filar said in a brief telephone interview that deep interest rate cuts, advocated by some as a way to ease buying pressure on the zloty, should also be ruled out, because such a radical loosening of the monetary reins could threaten price stability.  \par \par \uc2 "A radical interest rate cut is viewed by some as a method to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But I want to point out that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has an inflation target and a radical cut would threaten this target, so this is out of the question."  \par \par \uc2 Financial markets expect a modest cut in the bank's 4.50 percent benchmark rate later this month, convinced that the strong zloty will keep inflation well under control.  \par \par \uc2 But Prime Minister Kazimierz Marcinkiewicz and some members of his Law and Justice party have argued Polish rates should be closer to the euro zone's 2.25 percent, given that inflation in the EU newcomer stands at half of the euro area average.  \par \par \uc2 Filar, seen as a supporter of restrictive policy conditions on the bank's 10-member policy council and an advocate of fiscal discipline, said Poland's economic growth could suffer if the zloty held near its recent highs.  \par \par \uc2 "The recent (zloty) strengthening may pose problems for some exporters and could lead to weaker economic growth."  \par \par \uc2 The zloty, which hit a fresh multi-year high against the euro on Monday, has risen two percent so far this year and is up seven percent since early November.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-POLAND-FILAR (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|PX|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060114e21b000bx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
