\par\par \b \uc2 Poland - Factors to Watch on Nov 30  \b0\par\par\uc2 463 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2005\par 08:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Nov 30 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Poland's financial markets on Wednesday. ALL TIMES GMT (Poland GMT + 1 hour):  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  MEETING  \par \par \uc2 National Bank of Poland holds Monetary Policy Council announces its decision on interest rates after a monthly meeting. 15 of 21 analysts in a Reuters poll last week expected it to keep rates on hold for the third month running.  \par \par \uc2 BUDGET DEFICIT  \par \par \uc2 Poland's month-old conservative government on Tuesday kept its pre-election promise to financial market investors to lower the 2006 budget deficit, although doubts remain over the plan's details. [ID:nL29468397]  \par \par \uc2 Q3 GDP BEATS EXPECTATIONS  \par \par \uc2 Poland's economy grew faster than expected in the third quarter, quashing lingering expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could cut interest rates once more to boost the European Union newcomers' accelerating economy. [ID:nL29577480]  \par \par \uc2 BRE MERGES PENSION FUND  \par \par \uc2 BRE Bank said on Tuesday it will merge its pension fund unit with a larger fund owned by state-owned insurer PZU, completing a long-planned reduction of its role in the sector. [ID:nL29752442]  \par \par \uc2 PENSION BILL CHALLENGE  \par \par \uc2 Poland's conservative government decided on Tuesday to withdraw a legal challenge to a costly bill on miners' pensions but a leading business lobby said it would continue to fight to keep the measure from becoming law. [ID:nL29216383]  \par \par \uc2 EU PENSION FUND RULES  \par \par \uc2 Poland's Prime Minister Kazimierz Marcinkiewicz said on Tuesday he will try to convince the European Union to change the way it classifies Polish pension funds, which now stand to boost the newcomer's budget deficit. [ID:nL2961173]  \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA'S FOOD BAN  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  may ask the Euroepan Union for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the row over Russia's ban on imports of Polish meat is not resolved within weeks, a senior foreign ministry official was quoted as saying by daily Reczpospolita.  \par \par \uc2 LOT AIRLINES  \par \par \uc2 The Polish government will decide today whether it will replace the management board of Poland's national carrier LOT [LOT.UL], writes daily Rzeczpospolita.  \par \par \uc2 The current board wants a bourse debut for the state-controlled company by the second quarter of 2006.  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Natalia Reiter  \par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming events see [PL/DIARY] and a calendar of east European economic indicators see [CONV/DIARY].  \par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on:   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Polish equities       [PL-E]     E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  Polish money          [PL-M]     Polish debt           [PL-D]\par  Eastern Europe        [EEU]      All emerging markets  [EMRG]\par  Hot stocks            [HOT]      Stock markets         [STX]\par  Market debt news      [DBT]      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news            [FRX]\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For real-time index quotes, double click on: Warsaw WIG20 <.WIG20> Budapest BUX <.BUX> Prague PX50 <.PX50>  \f28 \par \par \uc2 LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|PX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051130e1bu000gq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
