\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Polish c.bank criticises Finmin's zloty, debt plans  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Wojciech Moskwa  \par \uc2 669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2005\par 12:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds Finance Minister Miroslaw Gronicki's comments)  \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Oct 12 (Reuters) - Poland's deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor on Wednesday criticised the finance ministry's plan to boost foreign borrowing and then to convert some of the money via the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market rather than through the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 In an interview, Jerzy Pruski said the growing reliance on foreign debt issues, set out in the finance ministry's medium-term debt strategy, could make Poland's path towards euro zone membership vulnerable to exchange-rate swings.  \par \par \uc2 But Finance Minister Miroslaw Gronicki stood firmly by the ministry's plans, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions were aimed at curbing debt servicing costs and not at a particular zloty impact.  \par \par \uc2 The zloty <EURPLN=> hit 40 month highs against the euro this week on expectations that the ministry will exchange part of the funds from Wednesday's $1.1 billion U.S. bond issue on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, not through the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it usually does.  \par \par \uc2 "In bilateral talks we have repeatedly warned the finance ministry of the negative economic aspects of this policy...of selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market and announcing further such \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Pruski said told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 "We have a floating exchange rate, where market forces shape the zloty rate, and here we have a non-market player interfering by its actions and announcements of future action which influence market expectations of future exchange rates."  \par \par \uc2 Pruski also said such interference was not needed because the zloty rate was currently strong. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has firmed 10 percent against the euro since 2005 lows hit in April.  \par \par \uc2 "One thing is certain -- the zloty is surely not too weak, regardless of how we assess its strength," he said. "Looking at the prospects for economic growth in Poland, appreciation brought about by such action is not needed."  \par \par \uc2 Gronicki defied the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's criticism and said the ministry might even sell all $1.1 billion from the U.S. issues to curb debt servicing costs if the zloty weakened sharply.  \par \par \uc2 "It will be aimed at minimising debt servicing costs and not at stabilising the zloty, because the latter is not the finance ministry's goal," Gronicki said.  \par \par \uc2 "Currently, our foreign debt is lower than in 2003, so the criticism from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not appropriate and partly emotional," he said.  \par \par \uc2 EURO RISK?  \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry's medium-term debt management strategy, published last week, envisages net foreign borrowing at 20 billion zlotys ($6.2 billion) next year with roughly 7 billion due to be exchanged into zloty on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 If the free-floating zloty weakens, the value of foreign debt in zloty terms would balloon, potentially boosting the value of total debt beyond limits needed for euro adoption.  \par \par \uc2 "In the context of meeting (euro zone entry) Maastricht criteria, a situation where our foreign debt is growing in relation to public debt is worrisome in itself, and surely exposes this ratio to exchange rate risk," Pruski said.  \par \par \uc2 Poland, which has said it wanted to join the euro area by 2010, expects its public debt to reach more than 52 percent of gross domestic product next year, and the weakening of the zloty could push it dangerously close to the EU's 60 percent cap.  \par \par \uc2 Financial market analysts also said the finance ministry's zloty-buying plans appeared odd given the unit's strength.  \par \par \uc2 "(Pruski's) statement points to increased tension between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the finance ministry over the ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  '\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 '," \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Bank BPH said in a report, calling the ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves "astonishing".  \par \par \uc2 Poland's economic growth has failed to pick up much speed after a sharp slowdown early this year, with exporters -- the main engine of growth -- complaining that zloty appreciation is pricing them out of markets. -- additional reporting by Pawel Sobczak  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-POLAND-PRUSKI (UPDATE 2, INTERVIEW)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|PX|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051012e1ac000qr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
